<!--Post: 7841--><!--Time: 1108707759-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7841"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 10:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A lot of people believe that the answer lies in the numbers.  This may be true with the numbers BTK writes and sends his communications, but it is my theory that the dates the murders happen on are more likely not any part of a numerology scheme.  BTK would want to commit the murders at a time that the routine of his victims are best for his tactics.   <BR> <BR>Then again... it does matter what MONTH he commits these in. <BR> <BR>For example:  Compare 1974 and 1977.  The spatial times between calendar months don&#39;t make much sense, but just add unsolved victims Baker, and Berardi. <BR> <BR>1974 <BR>-JANUARY 15 OTERO <BR>-APRIL 04 BRIGHT <BR>-November 12 Baker <BR> <BR>1977 <BR>-MARCH 17 VIAN <BR>-June 23 Berardi <BR>-DECEMBER 08 FOX <BR> <BR>Each year starts with a month, then has two months of rest, then another murder.  After five months of rest one more murder takes place. <BR> <BR>After that I can&#39;t see any other reasonable method.  Then again the &#34;hype&#34; died out by the Williams case that when Wegerle&#39;s case came around there wasn&#39;t much thought in it being BTK.  BTK changed after Anna William&#39;s decided to dance, rather than show up.  You can sense his disappointment in the poem.  Since the Anna Williams event happened in March, he could have attempted to repeat the &#34;pattern&#34; <BR> <BR> <BR>Of course all this is nothing if those two possible cases are not BTK&#39;s ... and they could very well not be.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7841-->
<!--Post: 7843--><!--Time: 1108708995-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7843"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 10:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes, but it is interesting how the known and possible BTK murders tend to cluster together, isn&#39;t it?  You can see it in armchairpi&#39;s timeline, too.  The idea that he would go through phases - periodic behavior for several months to a couple of years - and then &#34;go normal&#34; for a while, is quite reasonable.  The sex drives and sex lives of normal people show patterns - why not BTK as well?  I think your idea makes sense whether BTK was aware of it or not.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7843-->
<!--Post: 7852--><!--Time: 1108711053-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7852"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 11:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The three years difference could mean he was in the military and stationed somewhere else.  <BR> <BR>As I remember it, the military tour of duties used to be:  <BR> <BR>3 years for a CONUS assignment.  <BR> <BR>13 months for an un-accompanied assignment to Korea, and 18 months for un-accompanied tour of duty in the Panama Canal Zone, or Germany.  <BR> <BR>If the person was accompanied to either Korea, the Panama Canal Zone, or Germany &#40;meaning he brought his family along&#41;, then the tour of duty was 3 years for Germany and the CZ, and 24 months for Korea.  <BR> <BR>I have no idea how it was for Okinawa, Phillipines, Puerto Rico, Hawaii, or any other bases or posts, but I assume it would be like Germany. Someone will correct me on this, if I&#39;m wrong. Haha! <BR> <BR>These tour of duty minimums have changed during the years, but I know it was as I mentioned above in 1980s. This didn&#39;t account for extensions, or emergency leave, etc... <BR> <BR>;&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7852-->
<!--Post: 7882--><!--Time: 1108732769-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7882"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Hbtcontrol<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Hbtcontrol<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 18, 2005 - 5:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Of course, this is all true if we are assuming that these were the only murders by BTK during that time and I&#39;m not really sure &#40;and never have been&#41; that we can really make that assumption.  There may have been more and most likely were, in a different area, not yet attributed to him.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7882-->
